<h1>Week 25</h1>

<p><strong>From:</strong> Lana</p>
<p><strong>Artist:</strong> Depeche Mode</p>
<p><strong>Album:</strong> <em>Music for the Masses</em></p>

<p>Kayla,</p>

<p>
This week I chose <em>Music for the Masses</em> by Depeche Mode.
</p>

<p>
They used to be my number two favorite band when I was in my 20’s. I am not sure why I don’t like them as much now.
</p>

<p>
I literally played this cassette so many times. Listening to it now, I know what song comes next every single time.
</p>

<p>
Their music is dark and heavy, probably perfect for when I was filled with young adult angst. But now it makes me feel a little hopeless when I listen to it.
</p>

<p>
My number one favorite is “Behind the Wheel.”
</p>

<p>
Next are:
</p>

<ul>
<li>Never Let Me Down Again</li>
<li>To Have and To Hold</li>
</ul>

<p>
But really, it is all solid. This album definitely put them on the map.
</p>

<p>
I hope you like it.
</p>

<p>
Love you!!
</p>

<p>
Mom
</p>

